  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Following three days of intense political developments, Gibran Rakabuming Raka has formally stepped down as the Vice President of Indonesia. The resignation process concluded after he submitted an official letter to the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR), which confirmed the vacancy effective immediately upon receipt. In his departure address, the former Vice President expressed gratitude toward President Prabowo Subianto for the opportunity to serve and offered apologies for his tenure. The resignation has elicited diverse reactions within the Indonesian political landscape. Members of the Golkar faction have described the decision as an act of statesmanship. Conversely, representatives from the Indonesian Democratic Party of Struggle (PDIP) have questioned his motives, suggesting the resignation was a maneuver to preempt potential impeachment proceedings. The transition has also coincided with notable fluctuations in national economic indicators, including a decline in the value of the rupiah.",
